{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#469","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#469","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#469\",\"parent_revision\":\"287ebd07e5310d676abddc99f3f58a74ade13825\",\"root_revision\":\"71c9f6aa39cf95c64e38138cf0573153aba14305218112d5c2fcc50a7c9c8660\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_sync` and `backlog_pull` iterate over every open backlog item and make at least one GitHub API call per item. For a backlog with 50+ items, these operations can take 10\u201330 seconds and block the MCP connection.\\n\\nFastMCP v3 supports background task execution via `@mcp.tool(task=True)`. With this pattern, clients can initiate the operation and receive a task ID, then poll for completion. This prevents connection timeouts and allows other tools to remain available during the operation.\\n\\nFiles affected: `.claude/skills/backlog/backlog_core/server.py`\\n\\nPrerequisites:\\n- Tools must be converted to `async def` (see related item: Convert sync tools to async)\\n- `fastmcp[tasks]` extra must be added to pyproject.toml dependencies\\n- Progress reporting via `Progress` dependency (pairs with Context logging item)\\n\\nWork required:\\n- Add `fastmcp[tasks]` to pyproject.toml\\n- Convert backlog_sync and backlog_pull to `async def` with `task=True`\\n- Inject `Progress` dependency and call `progress.set_total(n)`, `progress.increment()` per item\\n\\nSource: FastMCP v3 docs `servers/tasks.mdx` \u2014 `@mcp.tool(task=True)` enables background execution; requires async functions and `fastmcp[tasks]` extra.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | FastMCP v3 `task=True` pattern verified | AVAILABLE | Item description cites `servers/tasks.mdx` |\\n| 2 | `fastmcp[tasks]` extra exists in FastMCP v3 | AVAILABLE | Item description cites FastMCP v3 docs |\\n| 3 | `backlog_sync` and `backlog_pull` are currently sync functions | DERIVABLE | Check `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` |\\n| 4 | Dependencies on sync tools from other code paths | DERIVABLE | Search for callers of backlog_sync/backlog_pull |\\n| 5 | FastMCP version currently in use | DERIVABLE | Check `pyproject.toml` fastmcp version |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information available or derivable.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add background task support to backlog_sync and backlog_pull via task=true** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: fastmcp-creator skill review of backlog_core/server.py\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Medium complexity. Affects MCP server connection behavior. Requires FastMCP v3 and async refactor.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `backlog_sync` and `backlog_pull` converted to `async def` with `@mcp.tool(task=True)`\\n- `fastmcp[tasks]` extra added to `pyproject.toml` dependencies for development-harness\\n- `Progress` dependency injected; each item processed calls `progress.increment()`\\n- Callers receive a task ID immediately; can poll for completion via FastMCP task status API\\n- Regression: existing sync callers that await the result directly still work (FastMCP task=True is backward-compat per docs)\\n- Tools remain functional \u2014 same inputs, same outputs, just async background execution\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 convert backlog_sync and backlog_pull to async with task=True\\n- `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` \u2014 add `fastmcp[tasks]` to dependencies\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a caller of `backlog_sync` or `backlog_pull` on a large backlog, I need these operations to run as background tasks with a task ID so the MCP connection does not block or timeout while iterating over 50+ GitHub API calls.\\n\",\"digest\":\"0de8bdb6243ff17d5cdd425d67ec0a7ff8d851c1efe621bfb4588dea19eb0610\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg0otA\"}"}